    "created_at": "2023-03-31T06:48:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-31T06:48:49Z",
    "body": "Well, yes, but we have [length](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#byte-sequence-length). And I feel less bad about using common-sense definitions if the base type is well-defined. So:\r\n\r\n- We can use [length](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#byte-sequence-length) instead of size\r\n- We can use \"Append\" because it's straightforwardly clear\r\n- For \"Extract\", I'd feel better if we broke it down into \"Let x be the first Y bytes of Z\", \"Remove the first Y bytes from Z\". Then the common-sense definitions are very clear.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
